eger is *odd* if it can be written as $2a+1,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is odd since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =-10q-5 \\\\  & =(-10b-6)+1 \\\\  & =2({{-5b-3}_{⏟}}_{a})+1 \\\\  & =2a+1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have defined $a=-5b-3,$ which is an integer."}]}
